# srt fork (deps/srt, inherited from upstream): CUDT::startup() guards its
# pthread_atfork registration with a plain function-local `static bool
# registered` (srtcore/api.cpp) instead of call_once, so concurrent
# srt_startup() calls data-race on the flag. Worst case is the atfork
# handler being registered twice; the actual refcounted global init
# (CUDTUnited::startup) is properly locked. Genuine fork bug - to be fixed
# in the srt fork repo (maxolgi/srt, branch quicsrt), then this entry gets
# deleted.
race:srt::CUDT::startup
